    {
      "id": "inugami-curse-s38-p1901",
      "source_en": "\"As soon as I had thought of the riddle, I carried his body to the boathouse, placed it in a boat, and rowed out of the sluice gate. I rowed near where the water seemed shallowest and plunged his body upside down into the mud. The ice was still not that thick then, but as the night wore on, it thickened and produced that ridiculous scene.\"",
